  "result": "Shell completion now keeps arguments that contain `#`. The tests in `tests/test_parser.py` and `tests/test_shell_completion.py` pass (67 passed). I didn't run the rest of the suite.\n\nThe fix is one line in `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py`: `lex.commenters = \"\"`. `shlex` treats `#` as a comment start by default, and that was cutting off everything from the first `#` onward. All four shells use this function, so the fix covers bash, zsh, fish and PowerShell.\n\nI added two cases to `test_split_arg_string` in `tests/test_parser.py`: `cli a#b` and `cli #x`. I didn't run them against the old code to confirm they failed first.\n\nI skipped the changelog entry because the repo has no `CHANGES.rst`.",
